From: z5vix <z5vix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Older GDK packages, the 2019 GDK's XPackage and Proton's EasyAntiCheat runtime

Applies after 0001. Found bringing up Gears 5 (2019 GDK, Microsoft Store build):
- appxinstall: GDK packages built before SegmentMetadata.bin store the game as a disk image (GPT with 4096-byte
  sectors, one NTFS volume). xvd_open now falls back to the volume's MFT when the user data has no segment table;
  members become lists of page runs, decrypted per region (resident files are kept in memory). Attribute lists and
  compressed, sparse or encrypted streams are refused rather than guessed at.
- xgameruntime: the 2019 GDK asks for IXPackageImpl as {be3f3e9f-c4b3-424d-9a95-d1af060559a5}; refusing it made
  Gears 5 exit silently right after XGameRuntimeInitialize. Unknown XPackage interfaces are now WARNed.
- ntdll: Proton's anti-cheat runtimes, as Proton does: PROTON_EAC_RUNTIME / PROTON_BATTLEYE_RUNTIME add the
  runtime's lib32/lib64 to the DLL path, and easyanticheat(_x86|_x64).dll loads the runtime's builtin bridge when
  the game ships EAC's Linux library (easyanticheat_x64.so) beside it, native otherwise. The bridge (built against
  Wine 7) looks up __wine_unix_call, which ntdll exports again for it. dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c and loadorder.c
  are new in this tree (upstream 11.20 plus these hunks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
